Subject: [PATCH 1/3] wl: decline A-MSDU inside A-MPDU to stop RX replay stalls

Under sustained load (100+ Mbit/s) the BCM4360 stops receiving: it stays
associated and keeps transmitting, but every unicast frame from the AP is
dropped as a CCMP replay (counters: rxdfrmucastmbss == rxundec == ccmpreplay)
until the station reconnects and gets fresh keys.

A/B tests show the closed binary mishandles the packet number of A-MSDUs that
arrive inside A-MPDUs. With rx_amsdu_in_ampdu=0 the stalls stop and throughput
is unchanged or better. The flag is only read when building the ADDBA response
(wlc_ampdu_recv_addba_req_resp), so setting it once after wlc_attach covers
every block-ack session. Declining A-MSDU in the ADDBA response is standard
802.11 behaviour.

The binary rejects this iovar unless its table entry has the whitelist flag
0x4000 (see unlock-iovars.py); without that the driver logs "FAILED" and
behaves as before.

New module option: rx_amsdu_in_ampdu (0 default, 1 Broadcom default, -1 untouched).

--- a/src/wl/sys/wl_linux.c
+++ b/src/wl/sys/wl_linux.c
@@ -219,6 +219,16 @@
 static int nompc = 0;
 module_param(nompc, int, 0);
 
+/* The closed part of the driver mishandles the CCMP packet number of A-MSDUs that
+ * arrive inside an A-MPDU: its stored receive counter jumps ahead and every later
+ * unicast frame is dropped as a replay (RX stalls under load until a reconnect).
+ * 0 = tell the AP not to send them (A-MSDU-supported bit cleared in our ADDBA
+ * response), 1 = Broadcom default, -1 = leave the driver's own setting.
+ * Needs the iovar whitelist bit set in wlc_hybrid.o (unlock-iovars.py). */
+static int rx_amsdu_in_ampdu = 0;
+module_param(rx_amsdu_in_ampdu, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_amsdu_in_ampdu, "accept A-MSDU inside A-MPDU (0 = no, default; 1 = Broadcom default)");
+
 #ifdef quote_str
 #undef quote_str
 #endif 
@@ -639,6 +649,13 @@
 	 * confirms this. */
 	wlc_iovar_setint(wl->wlc, "qtxpower", 23 * 4);
 
+	if (rx_amsdu_in_ampdu >= 0) {
+		int amsdu_err = wlc_iovar_setint(wl->wlc, "rx_amsdu_in_ampdu", !!rx_amsdu_in_ampdu);
+		printk(KERN_INFO "wl%d: rx_amsdu_in_ampdu=%d %s (bcmerror %d)\n", unit,
+		       !!rx_amsdu_in_ampdu, amsdu_err ? "FAILED, run unlock-iovars.py on wlc_hybrid.o" : "set",
+		       amsdu_err);
+	}
+
 #ifdef BCMDBG
 	if (macaddr != NULL) { 
 		int dbg_err;
